  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nA gray and gloomy start to the day betrayed those unfamiliar\nwith the forecast. Overcast skies and widespread fog have\ncleared as heights have risen and temperatures have soared. By\n1pm this afternoon, sunny skies have temps mostly in the \nupper-80s with dewpoints generally about 10 degrees lower. I'll\ndo the math for you... heat indices are mostly between 100 and \n108F. With the light winds, you'll have to manufacture your own \nway to remain cool. \n\nTemps tonight drop only into the lower to middle-70s, making it\ndifficult to cool homes with no A/C. \n\nA cluster of thunderstorms (MCS) is expected to work west to \neast through most of South Dakota this evening and may clip the\nnorthern portions of northeast Nebraska. These storms should be\nweakening as they approach the Iowa state line, but wind gusts \nover 70 mph are possible (5-10%). Expect those storms to clip \nthe area after dark, but mostly before midnight.",
